About
This repository contains a compact ESPHome alarm system concept for Home Assistant integration.
It targets hardware such as an Olimex ESP32-POE-ISO, a 128x32 OLED display, a custom keypad
built from 12 individual pushbuttons (digits 0-9 plus dedicated ARM/DISARM buttons) wired to
a second MCP23017, an RC522 NFC reader, and door contacts connected through a first MCP23017
I/O expander.

Important Notice
This project was created with the help of Anthropic's Claude (Claude Code).
The code is an experiment to demonstrate what AI-assisted development can build.
No warranty is provided for correctness, safety, or fitness for production use.
Use at your own risk.
